00:02:16,015 --> 00:02:18,718
We could do that since edges is

51
00:02:19,539 --> 00:02:20,874
an object here.

52
00:02:21,566 --> 00:02:24,044
We could do this here with a for-in loop.

53
00:02:25,740 --> 00:02:27,508
For const edge in

54
00:02:28,408 --> 00:02:28,794
edges

55
00:02:30,932 --> 00:02:31,447
or edge

56
00:02:32,845 --> 00:02:34,425
identifier in edges.

57
00:02:35,824 --> 00:02:37,564
With that, we can go through our edges here.

58
00:02:39,057 --> 00:02:40,945
And edges is an object where we have our

59
00:02:40,945 --> 00:02:43,414
node identifiers and then a list for every

60
00:02:43,414 --> 00:02:44,777
node with the connections

61
00:02:45,761 --> 00:02:46,858
and now in there

62
00:02:47,778 --> 00:02:49,892
we want a nested loop

63
00:02:51,505 --> 00:02:54,100
where we go through all the end nodes

64
00:02:55,112 --> 00:02:56,141
of the given

65
00:02:58,968 --> 00:02:59,274
edge

66
00:03:02,905 --> 00:03:05,951
and we check if end node is equal to the

67
00:03:05,951 --> 00:03:06,924
node identifier

68
00:03:08,011 --> 00:03:09,048
we want to remove.

69
00:03:10,798 --> 00:03:13,106
And if that's the case, we want to remove

70
00:03:13,138 --> 00:03:14,420
that node identifier.

71
00:03:15,478 --> 00:03:17,385
Now we got various ways of doing that. We

72
00:03:17,449 --> 00:03:20,190
could have our helper variable i here before

73
00:03:20,190 --> 00:03:22,450
we start looping through all the end nodes

74
00:03:22,659 --> 00:03:23,364
